strating complete achievement of the persuasion goal. The persuadee also expresses understanding of the benefits and implementation pathway, indicating deep conviction rather than superficial agreement. (5) Overall Assessment: This represents a textbook case of effective persuasion through rapport-building, evidence-based argumentation, responsive adaptation to concerns, and collaborative problem-solving. The persuader transformed initial ambivalence into enthusiastic acceptance while maintaining intellectual integrity and addressing legitimate concerns."
